<title>USA: Rains improve Mississippi crop outlook in week.</title>
<headline>Rains improve Mississippi crop outlook in week.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSON, Miss. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the weekly crop summary from the Mississippi Agricultural Statistics Service for the week ending Sunday, August 17.</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>According to the Mississippi Agricultural Statistics Service, there were 3.6 days suitable for fieldwork for the week ending August 17, 1997. The main farming activities for the week were insect and weed control. Boll weevil eradication has been effective; however, army worms are present in much of the state's crop acreage. Soil moisture conditions  were rated 1 percent very short, 8 percent short, 63 percent adequate and 28 percent surplus.</p>
